# demo-video fake-agent cassette — Codex TUI, the "asked" side of a delegation (Issue #2380)
#
# Format: <delayMs>|@input|@transcript|@hook <TAB> <payload>
#   - payload is expanded with `printf %b` (\e, \n, \t, \\)
#   - `{{TASK}}` is the first line of the message CommandMate sent (what
#     `commandmate ask … --instance codex` delivered); `@transcript` appends the
#     turn to the rollout file named by --transcript, stamped at replay time;
#     `@hook UserPromptSubmit` / `@hook Stop` report the turn's two ends to the
#     demo server the way codex's own hooks do, so `ask` settles on `Stop`
#     instead of holding 60 s for hooks that never answer
#   - the reply frame is held 8 s after `Stop`: the poller reads the pane
#     through a 5 s cache and the loop back to the banner must come after it
#
# Provenance: the frames are real `tmux capture-pane -p -e` captures of
# codex-cli 0.153.2 (200x1000, private tmux socket, disposable HOME) taken on
# 2026-09-04 for Issue #2310 — tests/fixtures/codex-live-2310/idle-composer.txt
# and turn-running.txt — with the working directory rewritten to the demo seed
# (padded to the original width so the banner box stays aligned) and the
# `1 background terminal running` tail dropped from the Working line. The reply
# lines follow the shape of a completed turn in
# tests/unit/lib/detection/fixtures/codex-live-1671/turn-complete-short-message.txt
# (`• <text>`, `─ Worked for …`, then the composer). The anchors the product
# keys on are byte-identical to the captures:
#   ready   -> the bold `›` composer glyph with the dim placeholder (SGR
#              attributes are what tell the composer `›` from the user-echo `›`,
#              #2310) and the model/directory footer
#   running -> `• Working (Ns • esc to interrupt)`
# Stripping the ANSI breaks real detection, so do not "tidy" this file. See
# SKILL.md > fixture の採取手順 to record a fresh one.
